  "live_records": {
    "q-129455": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129455",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(-\\frac{1}{3})=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+1-(-\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2-1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
