    "q-10205": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10205",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
