    "q-129599": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129599",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & y+3z=2 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-9=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-7)+2(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,x=-1+7-6=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-7$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-7,3⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
